Nivel de vechime: Nivel mediu de experiență
Tip de angajare: Full-time
Sectoare de activitate: Servicii IT și consultanță IT
Dear job seeker,
 We are looking for a Senior Data Engineer to join our team at fme Romania . In this role, you will be directly involved in delivering data and content migration projects, implementing data governance and data quality solutions, and supporting our clients in their digital transformation journey. You'll collaborate closely with both our customers and the fme delivery team to ensure successful outcomes.
At fme Romania , we work with clients across industries such as life sciences, finance, and manufacturing, providing professional advice, innovative solutions, and reliable support. This position offers you the chance to contribute to impactful projects while developing your expertise in data management.
 What you will do:
 Oversee the delivery of data and content migration projects, data governance, and data quality solutions; 
 Collaborate with clients and the fme delivery team on data-related initiatives to ensure project success; 
 Review existing migration tools and recommend improvements to enhance performance; 
 Develop and implement action plans to provide timely technical solutions for critical customer needs; 
 Stay current with new testing tools and strategies; 
 Act as a Subject Matter Expert (SME) for content migration solutions, supporting multiple projects simultaneously; 
 Lead migration projects, identify risks or issues early, and escalate them when needed
 Requirements
 Technical Skills:
 Proven experience with databases such as Oracle, Microsoft SQL Server, or PostgreSQL; 
 Hands-on experience in document/data migration with Enterprise Content Management Systems (e.g. SharePoint, OpenText Documentum, Box); 
 Familiarity with data migration tools (ETL) and ability to execute complex migration processes; 
 Strong troubleshooting, problem-solving, and analytical skills; 
 Experience working with validated systems, including producing quality documentation, installation procedures, and test cases; 
 Ability to collaborate with customers and teams across different geographical locations; 
 Self-driven mindset, with flexibility to adapt to fast-paced and ambiguous environments while remaining solution-focused. 
 Language:
 Excellent verbal and written communication skills in English;
 German is a plus. 
 Preferred qualifications:
 Bachelor's degree or higher in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field; 
 Experience migrating from and to Documentum content management systems to Veeva; 
 Knowledge of networking (TCP/IP, Internet protocols, load balancing, network configuration); 
 Good understanding of Java or other object-oriented programming languages; 
 Experience with Application Servers (WebLogic, WebSphere, JBoss, Tomcat)
 Benefits
 Here's our part of the deal: 
Be part of a mature, stable company with over 20 years in the market, combining long-term vision with modern engineering practices 
Work in an environment that supports your growth through an individual career plan and a dedicated learning & development budget 
Benefit from a comprehensive private health package, plus perks like WellHub, Bookster, and meal tickets 
Enjoy a comfortable, well-located office, easy to reach when working on-site 
Take advantage of a flexible work schedule that supports autonomy and work-life balance 
Connect with your colleagues through engaging company events and team activities 
 Why join us?
Growth opportunities: be part of a team that is expanding globally and contribute to our success;
Innovative environment: work with cutting-edge technology and industry trends;
Dynamic culture: thrive in a fast-paced, results-driven environment
 We are fme, an innovative company with over 20 years of experience in digital transformation, mature enough to handle complex projects, yet young at heart, providing a modern work environment for our team. As part of the fme Group , headquartered in Braunschweig, Germany, we have subsidiaries in Romania, the United States, and India.
Our mission is to help enterprises accelerate critical business processes, improve decision-making, and ensure information security and compliance using Enterprise Content Management, Business Intelligence, and Cloud technologies.
For over 20 years, fme Romania has grown through professionalism, adaptability, and collaboration. Get to know us: Watch our anniversary video .
